# Build output.
#
# A glob rather than a list of names. This file used to spell out every
# build directory individually, and the one that was not on the list --
# build-android-x86, created by hand for an emulator run -- was swept into
# the history by `git add -A`, taking a cross-compiled OpenSSL tree with
# it and costing 247 MB. Ignore the shape, not the instances: anything
# this project builds goes in a build-* directory.
build/
build-*/
.qmake.stash

# Cross-compiled dependency install prefixes (tool/build-deps-android.sh).
# Reproducible from the script, and several hundred MB if committed.
deps/

# The curated font set (tool/fetch-fonts.sh, project.md sec 9.2).
#
# Fetched, not committed: 54 MB of the set is font files and Iosevka alone
# is 42 MB of that, none of which ever diffs usefully. The script pins a
# version and a SHA-256 per family, which is the reproducibility a
# committed copy would have bought, and the licence texts it downloads
# alongside them are what sec 9.4's licences screen is built from.
fonts/

# Generated from the build machine's ncurses (the terminfo target,
# project.md sec 12.3p). Somebody else's data, so the tree carries the
# command that produces it rather than the file itself -- the same trade
# fonts/ makes just above.
terminfo/
android/assets/terminfo/

# The built binary, copied out of build/ by `make`
/beerssh
/beersshd

# Python bytecode from tool/
__pycache__/

# Editor and OS litter
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store

# debhelper's working state. `debian/` holds the packaging sources only;
# everything below is generated by dpkg-buildpackage and must not be
# committed -- a stale substvars or files list silently changes what the
# next package declares.
debian/.debhelper/
debian/files
debian/tmp/
debian/beerssh/
debian/beerssh-fonts/
debian/*.substvars
debian/*.debhelper.log
debian/debhelper-build-stamp

# The manual page and the bash completion. Both generated from the option
# table by the binary (project.md sec 8.6), so committing either would be
# committing a copy of the parser that is free to disagree with it.
beerssh.1
beerssh.bash
beersshd.1
.fmake/
